"\"Nourish water to moisten wood\" runs the same logic through a different pair: water, associated with the kidney, is traditionally understood to generate wood, associated with the liver, along the generating cycle — so a liver showing signs of dryness or excess heat can be treated by nourishing the kidney that feeds it, rather than only cooling the liver directly. Between this lesson and the earlier one on mother-child treatment, the two cycles this unit opened with turn out to double as two separate treatment toolkits, not just two diagrams describing how the five elements relate to each other in theory.": "5a236b25a5c5",
